-- title:
--   Lemma 7, p. 5 — refinement of a simple cone with x⊤Hx ≥ 0 into simple cones whose zero-minimum faces have a zero extreme ray
-- statement:
--   Let $C = \operatorname{cone}\{r^1,\dots,r^d\}\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ be a simple pointed cone, given by linearly independent rational generators, and let $H\in\mathbb Q^{n\times n}$ satisfy $x^\top Hx\ge0$ for every $x\in C$. Let $f\in\mathbb Q^n$ satisfy $f^\top r^j>0$ for every $j$, so that $\mathcal H = \{x : f^\top x = 1\}$ is a normalizing hyperplane for $C$ (as the hyperplane of Lemma 6 is). There is a single polynomial $g$, fixed before $n$, $d$ and the data, such that there are finitely many simple cones $C^i = \operatorname{cone}\{g^{i1},\dots,g^{id}\}$ with rational generators and
--
--   (a) $\bigcup_i C^i = C$;
--
--   (b) for every $i$ and every face $F$ of $C^i$ — that is, $F = \operatorname{cone}\{g^{ij} : j\in S\}$ for a subset $S$ of the generators — if
--   $$\min\{x^\top Hx : x\in F\cap\mathcal H\} = 0$$
--   (the minimum is attained and equals $0$), then $F$ has an extreme ray $v = g^{ij}$, $j\in S$, with $v^\top Hv = 0$;
--
--   (c) every $C^i$ has $d$ linearly independent generators (so $\dim C^i = \dim C$), each of bit-size at most $g\big(\operatorname{size}(H)+\sum_j\operatorname{size}(r^j)+\operatorname{size}(f)\big)$.
--
--   The refinement isolates the directions along which the quadratic form vanishes; it is the step that lets the proof of Theorem 1 treat the zero directions linearly.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The faces of a simple cone are exactly the cones of subsets of its generators, and the extreme rays of such a face are spanned by those generators. The empty face meets $\mathcal H$ in the empty set and imposes nothing.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: "$\mathcal H$ the normalizing hyperplane from Lemma 6" and "$\{H,C\}$-small complexity" → any rational $f$ with $f^\top r^j>0$ for all $j$, with the bound polynomial in the size of $\{H, r^1,\dots,r^d, f\}$; reason: the hyperplane of Lemma 6 satisfies $f^\top x\ge 1/R>0$ on unit vectors of $C$, hence $f^\top r^j>0$, and its size is polynomial in that of the generators, so composing the polynomials gives the source's $\{H,C\}$-small bound.
--   - encoding: "simple pointed cone $C$" and its complexity → $C$ generated by linearly independent rational vectors, complexity measured on the generators; reason: a simple cone is the cone of its linearly independent extreme rays, and facet and vertex complexity are polynomially related (Schrijver, Thm 10.2, cited on p. 5).
--   - encoding: "face $F$ of $C^i$", "extreme ray $v$ of $F$", "dimension of $C^i$ equals that of $C$" → cones of subsets $S$ of the generators, a generator $g^{ij}$ with $j\in S$, and $d$ linearly independent generators; reason: these are the faces, extreme rays and dimension of a simple cone.
--   - encoding: "$\min\{\dots\}=0$" → $0$ is the least element of the set of values; reason: a minimum is an attained infimum.
-- source:
--   Del Pia, Dey & Molinaro, Mixed-integer quadratic programming is in NP, arXiv:1407.4798v1, p. 5, Lemma 7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MIQPInNP_SmallSol_Setting

namespace MIQPInNP.SmallSol

/-- Lemma 7, p. 5 (Del Pia, Dey & Molinaro, arXiv:1407.4798v1). -/
theorem lemma_7 :
    ∃ g : Polynomial ℕ, ∀ (n d : ℕ) (H : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℚ) (r : Fin d → Fin n → ℚ)
      (f : Fin n → ℚ),
      LinearIndependent ℝ (fun j => toReal (r j)) →
      (∀ x ∈ cone (Set.range fun j => toReal (r j)), 0 ≤ quadForm H x) →
      (∀ j, 0 < ∑ k, (f k : ℝ) * toReal (r j) k) →
      ∃ (N : ℕ) (gens : Fin N → Fin d → Fin n → ℚ),
        (⋃ i, cone (Set.range fun j => toReal (gens i j))) =
          cone (Set.range fun j => toReal (r j)) ∧
        (∀ (i : Fin N) (S : Finset (Fin d)),
          IsLeast (quadForm H ''
              (cone ((fun j => toReal (gens i j)) '' (S : Set (Fin d))) ∩ hyperplane f)) 0 →
            ∃ j ∈ S, quadForm H (toReal (gens i j)) = 0) ∧
        (∀ i, LinearIndependent ℝ (fun j => toReal (gens i j)) ∧
          ∀ j, vecSize (gens i j) ≤ g.eval (matSize H + ∑ k, vecSize (r k) + vecSize f)) := by sorry

end MIQPInNP.SmallSol
